From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:27:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: iomfb_m4: log rejected allocate_buffer
 requests

On J604 (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M4, firmware 26.6.2) the first D451
allocate_buffer callback after IOMFB start fails with -EINVAL and
quarantines the retained session:

  DCP callback D451 tag=31353444 20/28 remote=0 flag9=0 dispatch failed: -22

The callback shape (20/28) matches the table. No "Retaining shared DCP
backing" line follows, so the DART allocator did not fail after
publication. That leaves the request validation in
dcp_m4_memory_callback(): the 0x703 type word, the size bound, the
alignment exponent (4 on the qualified firmware) or bytes 16-18.

Log the 20 request bytes when a D451 callback is rejected, so the
J604 request can be compared with the qualified one before the
validation is extended. The request carries only sizes and flags.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 79d82b0e5e7c9de533b2a9ad3a7a20c4e399f4c9)
[j604: k610 drm sync: iomfb_m4.c conflict with the upstream external-DCP D-call logging in dcp_m4_runtime_memory(); the rejected allocate_buffer log comes first, the upstream external warnings stay as else-branches.]
(cherry picked from commit 901106b00da8cae22e576e58e029fdfdf1a6ae10)
(cherry picked from commit 2d0557d1a0368de7ce6992fa4142d16106737ebb)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 6997db3db5..c2b96cf22b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -1188,7 +1188,10 @@ static int dcp_m4_runtime_memory(void *cookie, unsigned int method,
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = dcp_m4_memory_callback(dcp->memory, &dcp_m4_memory_ops, dcp, method, input, output);
-	if (dcp->external && ret)
+	/* 20 bytes of sizes and flags: log them so a rejected shape can be qualified. */
+	if (ret && method == 451)
+		dev_err(dcp->dev, "allocate_buffer request rejected: %d in=%20ph\n", ret, input);
+	else if (dcp->external && ret)
 		dev_warn(dcp->dev, "D%03u failed: %d (PIODMA %s)\n", method, ret,
 			 dcp->piodma ? "present" : "absent");
 	else if (dcp->external && method == 201 && get_unaligned_le32(out + 12))
